1
00:03:06,666 --> 00:03:12,666
Kiss your nerves goodbye!

2
00:06:13,333 --> 00:06:19,333
Evil Dead II is a horror, comedy, fantasy film directed by Sam Raimi.

3
00:09:20,000 --> 00:09:26,000
Ash Williams and his girlfriend Linda find a log cabin in the woods with a voice recording from an archeologist who had recorded himself
reciting ancient chants from "The Book of the Dead." As they play the recording an evil power is unleashed taking over Linda's body.

4
00:12:26,666 --> 00:12:32,666
Ash, played by Bruce Campbell.

5
00:15:33,333 --> 00:15:39,333
Annie, played by Sarah Berry.

6
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:46,000
Jake, played by Dan Hicks.

7
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:52,666
Bobby Joe, played by Kassie DePaiva.

8
00:24:53,333 --> 00:24:59,333
Possessed Henrietta, played by Ted Raimi.

9
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Linda, played by Denise Bixler.

10
00:31:06,666 --> 00:31:12,666
Evil Dead II (also known in publicity materials as Evil Dead 2: Dead by Dawn) is a 1987 American
comedy horror film directed by Sam Raimi, who co-wrote it with Scott Spiegel.

11
00:34:13,333 --> 00:34:19,333
It is the sequel to The Evil Dead (1981) and the second
installment in the Evil Dead franchise.

12
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:26,000
It stars Bruce Campbell as Ash Williams, who vacations with
his girlfriend to a remote cabin in the woods.

13
00:40:26,666 --> 00:40:32,666
He discovers an audio tape of recitations from a book of ancient texts, and when the
recording is played, it unleashes a number of demons which possess and torment him.

14
00:43:33,333 --> 00:43:39,333
After the critical and commercial failure of Crimewave (1985), Raimi, producer Robert Tapert, and Campbell
began work on a sequel to The Evil Dead at the insistence of their publicist Irvin Shapiro.

15
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:46,000
Having endorsed the original film, author Stephen King brought the project to the attention of producer Dino
De Laurentiis, with whom he had been making his directorial debut Maximum Overdrive (1986).

16
00:49:46,666 --> 00:49:52,666
De Laurentiis agreed to provide financial backing, and assigned the filmmakers a
considerably larger budget than they had worked with on the original film.

17
00:52:53,333 --> 00:52:59,333
Although Raimi had devised a premise set in the Middle Ages and involving time travel,
De Laurentiis requested that the film be similar to its predecessor.

18
00:56:00,000 --> 00:56:06,000
Evil Dead II was shot in Wadesboro, North Carolina and Detroit, Michigan in 1986, and featured extensive stop-motion animation and prosthetic makeup effects created
by a team of artists that included Mark Shostrom, Greg Nicotero, Robert Kurtzman and Tom Sullivan, the latter of whom returned from the original film.

19
00:59:06,666 --> 00:59:12,666
The finished film was released in the United States on March 13, 1987; due to its high level of violence, it was released
through a pseudonymous distributor to curb an anticipated X rating from the Motion Picture Association of America.

20
01:02:13,333 --> 01:02:19,333
Much like The Evil Dead, it was widely acclaimed by critics, who praised its humor, Raimi's direction, and Campbell's performance;
many have considered it superior to its predecessor and similarly as one of the greatest horror films ever made.

21
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:26,000
Despite being given a somewhat limited release, it was a minor box
office success, grossing just under $6 million.

22
01:08:26,666 --> 01:08:32,666
As with the first film, Evil Dead II has accumulated a
large, international cult following.

23
01:11:33,333 --> 01:11:39,333
In 1992, it was followed by the direct sequel Army of Darkness, which utilized Raimi's original premise; in 2013, it was followed by
the soft reboot and continuation Evil Dead; and in 2015, it was followed by the television series Ash vs Evil Dead.

24
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:46,000
A fifth film in the series, Evil Dead Rise, was released on April 21, 2023.

25
01:17:46,666 --> 01:17:52,666
The film explores themes of deer, tape recorder,
chainsaw, spirit, cabin in the woods.

26
01:20:53,333 --> 01:20:59,333
The tone is lighthearted and dark.
